  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3.1. Increased capacity of member States to formulate and implement a new generation of gender-responsive national employment policies, including for youth</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In September 2020, the Ministry of Public Service and Labour coordinated the first inter-ministerial NEP Committee to review implementation progress and co-ordination mechanisms for the National Employment Policy (NEP) adopted in August 2018. The NEP is aligned with the Government&apos;s medium term plan (National Strategy for Transformation, which seeks to facilitate creation of 1.5 million decent and productive jobs by 2024) and is implemented in consultation with Social partners, Private Sector Federation (PSF) and Rwanda Workers&apos; Trade Union Confederation (CESTRAR), as well as other stakeholders In August 2021, ILO provided technical support to 30 members of the NEP inter-ministerial committee to conduct field visits to various districts to monitor and evaluate the progress by public institutions towards the 1.5 million jobs target. Institutions represented included Private Sector Federation (Employer Organization &#x2013; PSF), Rwanda Development Board, Ministry of Finance and Economic Planning, Ministry of Agriculture, Ministry of Local Government, Ministry of Public Service and Labour and Ministry of Youth and Culture.

In addition, in September 2020, the ILO supported the Ministry of Public Service and Labour to conduct the first NEP co-ordination meeting and Employment Mainstreaming training for Directors of planning in sector ministries, NEP technical team in the Ministry of Public Service and Labour, and Business development director in all the country&apos;s 30 districts.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">3.1.1. Number of member States with new generation of national employment policies addressing country-specific future of work challenges</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
